  {
   "title": "Staying: questions and negatives",
   "body": "",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "You're not staying here.",
     "es": "No te quedas aquí."
    },
    {
     "en": "Why aren't you staying here?",
     "es": "¿Por qué no te quedas aquí?"
    }
   ],
   "t": 0
  },
  {
   "title": "quedarme after another verb",
   "body": "With a 'to' form, the little word attaches to the end. Siete (seven) is like the 'set-' in setiembre/septiembre, with the e split.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I'm going to stay until seven.",
     "es": "Voy a quedarme hasta las siete."
    },
    {
     "en": "Do you want to stay?",
     "es": "¿Quieres quedarte?"
    }
   ],
   "t": 36.9
  },
  {
   "title": "deber → debemos",
   "body": "Match the little word to the person: debemos quedarnos (ourselves).",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "We must stay.",
     "es": "Debemos quedarnos. / Nos debemos quedar."
    }
   ],
   "t": 112.7
  },
  {
   "title": "tener que: less serious than deber",
   "body": "",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "You have to stay here.",
     "es": "Tienes que quedarte aquí."
    },
    {
     "en": "I want to know why you have to stay here.",
     "es": "Quiero saber por qué tienes que quedarte aquí."
    }
   ],
   "t": 154.9
  },
  {
   "title": "poder: puedo, podemos",
   "body": "No split in the we form.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I can't stay tonight.",
     "es": "No puedo quedarme esta noche."
    },
    {
     "en": "We can't stay tonight.",
     "es": "No podemos quedarnos esta noche."
    }
   ],
   "t": 230.9
  },
  {
   "title": "piensas + verb = plan to",
   "body": "",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "Do you plan on staying here tonight?",
     "es": "¿Piensas quedarte aquí esta noche?"
    }
   ],
   "t": 325.0
  },
  {
   "title": "Use logic, not feel",
   "body": "Place the little word by the rule (before the changed verb), not by what sounds good. A mistake made through logic fixes the logic.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I have stayed.",
     "es": "Me he quedado."
    },
    {
     "en": "We haven't stayed.",
     "es": "No nos hemos quedado."
    },
    {
     "en": "Haven't YOU stayed?",
     "es": "¿Tú no te has quedado?"
    }
   ],
   "t": 347.5
  },
  {
   "title": "llamar; me llamo = my name is",
   "body": "Llamar = to call / phone. Introducing yourself, Spanish says 'I call myself'.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "My name is …",
     "es": "Me llamo …"
    },
    {
     "en": "What's your name?",
     "es": "¿Cómo te llamas?"
    }
   ],
   "t": 459.3
  }
